# SSH host key pins for hosts managed from CI.
#
# These are PUBLIC keys — committing them is deliberate. Pinning them in the
# repository is what lets GitHub Actions keep `host_key_checking` enabled: an
# ephemeral runner has no ~/.ssh/known_hosts of its own, so without this file
# the only alternatives are trust-on-first-use (accepts any key, i.e. accepts a
# MITM) or disabling host key checking entirely.
#
# Regenerate / add a host with:
#
#     ssh-keyscan -t ed25519,ecdsa,rsa <hostname> | sort >> ansible/known_hosts
#
# and review the diff before committing. A changed key here means either you
# rebuilt the server or someone is intercepting the connection — never update
# it blindly.
#
